y seem noticeably empty but a  lot of the basics stayed open the entire  time suburbs  not even have been as dramatically  different I it's hard for me to say for  sure so the answers in terms of how much  longer can we stay quote shut down it's  very clear that there is not a lot of  political appetite even in the more  liberal states to stay shut even a  single day longer than public health  officials say that we should so I think  we're increasingly going to start seeing  two tiers we were going to start to see  places that had early hot spots and took  it very seriously New York and  Massachusetts in California are the ones  I'm most familiar with that in the next  two weeks to four weeks two to three  weeks are going to be able to start  opening some things with caution  still with masks indoors outdoors when  you can't social distance but there will  be some opening up more than likely  manufacturing hopefully can start to  come back with people wearing masks and  distancing in factories etc the  governor's will sort of figure it out  the problem is that we are starting to  see rapidly rising cases in places like  Florida Georgia Texas and there are  others although I don't have the numbers  readily sort of in my mind and on a  percentage basis they are seeing faster  and faster increases in cases they're  not going to be able to open up or if  they do it is going to be significantly  tragic significantly tragic so you have  some states starting to say we're going  to start running out of unemployment  insurance money that's going to be  pressure especially for Republican  governors who are very concerned with  debt in this abstract sense to try to  open up the saddest part about all of it  and ultimately these are decisions that  governors will have to make and the  answer as many of them are going to  start opening some things in the next  two to three weeks sadly if on March 5th  when we had over 200 cases Trump had  said from the federal government I need 